    @normalize_token.register(Enum)
    def normalize_enum(e):
        return type(e).__name__, e.name, e.value

immediately after the `normalize_token = Dispatch()` line, we extend the dispatcher to handle Enum types. This implementation returns each enum’s type name, member name, and value in a tuple—matching the PR’s suggestion—and integrates seamlessly with the existing normalization pattern to guarantee reproducible hashing for Enums.

